    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d768">

                <pb facs="0788" n="784" xml:id="pg784"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.811/1115: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Peck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-05-10T16:00:00+07:00">May 10, 1939—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 10—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>322. The Embassy has today received a note from the Foreign Office quoting a
                    communication from the Military Affairs Commission to the effect that the mouth
                    of the West River in Kwangtung has been closed and that the entrance and exit of
                    Chinese and foreign vessels is prohibited.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Embassy at Peiping, Canton, Hong Kong. Latter please notify American
                    naval authorities and shippers at Canton and Hong Kong.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
